.\" openi2pd: i2pd.1.
.\"
.\" Configures project configuration and integration.
.\"

.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt I2PD 1
.Os openi2pd
.Sh NAME
.Nm i2pd
.Nd openi2pd I2P router daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -conf Ar file
.Op Fl -datadir Ar directory
.Op Fl -daemon
.Op Fl -foreground
.Op Fl -service
.Op Fl -log Ar destination
.Op Fl -loglevel Ar level
.Op Ar options ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the openi2pd router for the I2P anonymous network.
It builds encrypted tunnels, maintains the network database, and provides
local HTTP and SOCKS proxies plus optional client services.
The router is a long-running daemon and does not require a terminal.
.Pp
The administrative web console has been removed.
Use
.Xr i2pd-tui 1
for local, authenticated administration over a UNIX-domain socket.
.Pp
Except for
.Fl -help
and
.Fl -version ,
long command-line options use the same names as configuration keys without
the leading
.Ql -- .
Command-line values take precedence over
.Pa i2pd.conf .
The
.Fl --help
output is the authoritative list for the installed build.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the option summary and exit.
.It Fl -version
Print router, Boost and TLS library versions and exit.
.It Fl -conf Ar file
Read the main configuration from
.Ar file .
.It Fl -tunconf Ar file
Read client and server tunnel definitions from
.Ar file .
.It Fl -tunnelsdir Ar directory
Read additional tunnel definitions from
.Ar directory .
.It Fl -certsdir Ar directory
Read certificates used for SU3 and family verification from
.Ar directory .
.It Fl -datadir Ar directory
Store router keys, profiles, the network database and local state in
.Ar directory .
.It Fl -pidfile Ar file
Write the daemon process ID to
.Ar file .
.It Fl -log Ar destination
Select
.Ar stdout ,
.Ar file ,
or
.Ar syslog .
.It Fl -logfile Ar file
Write file logs to
.Ar file .
.It Fl -loglevel Ar level
Set the minimum level to
.Ar debug ,
.Ar info ,
.Ar warn ,
.Ar error ,
or
.Ar none .
.It Fl -logclftime
Use full CLF-formatted timestamps in file logs.
.It Fl -daemon
Detach and run in the background.
.It Fl -foreground
Stay in the foreground even if the configuration enables daemon mode.
Service definitions use this option so the service manager retains the
router process.
.It Fl -service
Use system service directories and defaults.
.It Fl -ipv4 , Fl -ipv6
Enable or disable the corresponding address family.
.It Fl -host Ar address
Publish an external address.
.It Fl -port Ar port
Use a fixed incoming transport port.
.It Fl -ifname Ar name , Fl -ifname4 Ar name , Fl -ifname6 Ar name
Bind transport sockets to a named interface.
.It Fl -nat
Assume that the router is behind NAT.
.It Fl -bandwidth Ar class
Select a bandwidth class such as
.Ar L ,
.Ar O ,
.Ar P ,
or
.Ar X .
.It Fl -floodfill
Participate in the network database as a floodfill router.
.It Fl -notransit
Do not accept transit tunnels at startup.
.It Fl -ntcp2.enabled Ar bool
Enable or disable the NTCP2 transport.
.It Fl -ssu2.enabled Ar bool
Enable or disable the SSU2 transport.
.It Fl -ntcp2.port Ar port , Fl -ssu2.port Ar port
Set transport-specific listening ports.
.It Fl -httpproxy.enabled Ar bool
Enable or disable the local HTTP proxy.
.It Fl -httpproxy.address Ar address
Bind the HTTP proxy to a local address.
.It Fl -httpproxy.port Ar port
Bind the HTTP proxy to a local port.
.It Fl -socksproxy.enabled Ar bool
Enable or disable the local SOCKS proxy.
.It Fl -socksproxy.address Ar address
Bind the SOCKS proxy to a local address.
.It Fl -socksproxy.port Ar port
Bind the SOCKS proxy to a local port.
.It Fl -i2pcontrol.enabled Ar bool
Enable or disable the local I2PControl service.
.It Fl -i2pcontrol.address Ar address
Bind I2PControl to a local address.
.It Fl -i2pcontrol.port Ar port
Bind I2PControl to a local port.
.It Fl -i2pcontrol.password Ar password
Set the I2PControl password.
Prefer the configuration file and restrictive permissions over a command line
that may be visible in the process list.
.It Fl -tui.enabled Ar bool
Enable or disable the local TUI socket.
.It Fl -tui.socket Ar path
Set the UNIX-domain socket used by
.Xr i2pd-tui 1 .
.It Fl -privsep.enabled Ar bool
Enable supported privilege-separation workers.
The log worker and the opt-in torrent/router storage workers use separate
processes; networking, crypto and the router core are not separated by this
option.
.It Fl -privsep.log Ar bool
Route file logging through the isolated log worker.
On .Ox the supervisor is spawned while the startup pledge still permits
.Fn exec ;
the runtime core retains
.Va proc
but never
.Va exec .
.It Fl -reseed.file Ar path-or-url
Reseed from a local SU3 file or an HTTPS URL.
.It Fl -reseed.urls Ar urls
Use the comma-separated reseed service URLs.
.It Fl -upnp.enabled Ar bool
Enable or disable UPnP port mapping.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.i2pd/i2pd.conf
Per-user configuration on Linux and other non-service installations.
.It Pa /etc/i2pd/i2pd.conf
System configuration on .Ox and packaged Linux installations.
.It Pa /var/lib/i2pd
Default Linux service data directory.
.It Pa /var/i2pd
Default .Ox service data directory.
.It Pa i2pd.pid
Process ID file, relative to the data directory unless configured otherwise.
.It Pa i2pd-tui.sock
Default local TUI socket, relative to the data directory.
.El
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Dv SIGHUP
Reload tunnel configuration.
.It Dv SIGUSR1
Reopen an in-process file log for rotation.
This is a no-op for stdout, syslog and
.Va privsep.log
logging; use copy-truncate rotation for the isolated log worker.
.It Dv SIGINT
Perform a graceful shutdown, draining transit tunnels.
.It Dv SIGTERM , Dv SIGABRT
Perform an orderly shutdown without the transit-tunnel grace period.
.It Dv SIGTSTP
Disconnect from the network when
.Va unix.handle_sigtstp
is enabled.
.It Dv SIGCONT
Restore network operation after
.Dv SIGTSTP .
.El
.Sh SECURITY
The daemon must run as an unprivileged user.
The local TUI socket is created with mode 0600 and accepts only peers with the
daemon's effective UID.
The router exposes no administrative HTTP interface.
.Pp
On .Ox the daemon uses
.Xr pledge 2
and
.Xr unveil 2
where configured.
Do not disable or broaden the sandbox to work around a path or service
configuration error.
The optional JSON-RPC torrent listener is loopback-only and disabled by
default; it is not a web console.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run a foreground router with a private data directory:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
i2pd --datadir "$HOME/.i2pd" --log stdout
.Ed
.Pp
Start the .Ox service:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
rcctl enable i2pd
rcctl start i2pd
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr i2pd-tui 1 ,
.Xr i2pdctl 1 ,
.Xr pledge 2 ,
.Xr unveil 2 ,
.Xr rcctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
is derived from the PurpleI2P i2pd router and is maintained by the openi2pd
project.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An -nosplit
.An openi2pd
